'' linux-arm64: "frame-pointer"="non-leaf" on every definition, the same rule as macos-arm64's
'' (docs/tiko-linux-arm64 D-L1-3). clang 23 writes "non-leaf-no-reserve" for aarch64-linux,
'' which also keeps a frame record in every non-leaf function and only frees x29 in leaves; one
'' spelling for both arm64 targets keeps x29 always reserved. See FrameAttr_ in
'' src/codegen/llvmemit.tiko.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target linux-arm64 --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/frame-pointer.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: define i32 @"OUTER"(i32 %p0) nounwind uwtable(sync) "frame-pointer"="non-leaf" {
'' EXPECT-OUT: define i32 @"INNER"(i32 %p0) nounwind uwtable(sync) "frame-pointer"="non-leaf" {
'' EXPECT-OUT: define i32 @"main"(i32 %p0, ptr %p1) nounwind uwtable(sync) "frame-pointer"="non-leaf" {
